# AI Knowledge Engine — deployed KB .gitignore
# Copy to your KB root as `.gitignore` (rename, removing .template).
#
# Private by default: source files, converted text, review queues and
# session logs stay on this machine even after `git add -A`. To version one
# of them (for example to carry raw/ to another machine through a PRIVATE
# remote), delete its line below. Never push such a repository anywhere
# public — raw/ and interactions/ hold chats, personal context and secrets.

# Virtual env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Private material (see kb-docs/03_PIPELINE.md and kb-docs/04_REVIEW.md).
# Leading "/" = base root only: knowledge/**/assets/ etc. stay versioned.
/raw/
/assets/
/processed/
/review/
/interactions/

# Machine-local state: locks, caches, hook logs
/.kb-state/
# Session hand-off, regenerated by scripts/kb_status.py on every reindex
/STATUS.md

# Repomix output (regenerated locally)
/.repomix/

# Operational state (regenerated, not source of truth)
/.last_consolidation
/.last_reflection
/.watcher.pid
/.watcher.log

# Lint reports (regenerated)
/lint-report.md

# Snapshots: heal backups (see kb-docs/18_HEAL.md) and finalize.sh
# leftovers (kb_upgrade's --accept/--force backups live in .kb-state/upgrade-backups/)
/.kb-backups/
/.kb-finalize-backup/
/.kb-finalize.journal

# Cross-base sync workspace (see kb-docs/16_MERGE.md). Bundles are large
# binaries and backups are machine-local; the merge reports are worth keeping
# if you version the base — drop the last line to do that.
/sync/inbox/
/sync/outbox/
/sync/applied/
/sync/backups/
/sync/reports/

# Optional: the operations log is private too. Uncomment to exclude it.
# log.md

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
